{
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "id": "29715_hageru",
  "headword": "{剥|は}げる",
  "reading": "はげる",
  "romaji": "hageru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-ichidan",
  "gloss": "to peel off; to come off; to fade",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to peel off; to come off; to fade (of paint, coating, color)",
      "explanation": "For a surface layer such as paint, coating, plating, or color to come away or wear off, leaving the base exposed. Intransitive: the layer comes off by itself rather than being removed by someone."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29715_hageru_ex1",
      "japanese": "ペンキが{剥|は}げる。",
      "english": "The paint peels off.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29715_hageru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{壁|かべ}の{塗装|とそう}が{剥|は}げてきた。",
      "english": "The paint on the wall has started to peel.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29715_hageru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{長年|ながねん}{使|つか}って、{鍋|なべ}のコーティングが{剥|は}げてしまった。",
      "english": "After years of use, the pot's coating has peeled off.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n{剥|は}げる is intransitive—a coating or color comes off on its own. The transitive pair is {剥|は}がす (to peel/strip something off). The near-synonym {剥|は}がれる also intransitive, but tends to describe a sheet-like layer lifting away, while {剥|は}げる stresses coating, plating, or color wearing off and fading.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{剥|は}げている describes the resultant state—the surface is now bare where the layer has come off.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {色|いろ}が{剥|は}げる: the color fades/comes off\n- メッキが{剥|は}げる: the plating comes off; figuratively, someone's true nature shows through\n- {日焼|ひや}けが{剥|は}げる: a suntan peels\n\nNOTE:\nDo not confuse with the homophone {禿|は}げる (to go bald), which is written with a different kanji.",
